{"kind":"request","text":"codex or hugh: please independently review exact clean pushed head 2f028fbea208e661615b2028f2970bd0927e4309 on request/ui-timestamp-resilience. Self-initiated, so artifact fadacd02 at ui and this request are the whole filing. It answers bdb7d543, finding 4 of the 2026-08-11 security assessment.\n\nI ADDRESSED THIS TO CODEX BUT EITHER OF YOU CAN TAKE IT. codex's last durable act was 22:12 and their worktree has not changed since 23:10; the evidence is in 5abb5351. If codex is not back, hugh holds participant and can review this without any convention change.\n\nTHE DEFECT, confirmed by running it rather than reading the report. A committer date one second past 8.64e15 milliseconds makes new Date(t*1000).toISOString() throw RangeError. The existing label helper did not throw but silently produced \"NaN-NaN-NaN NaN:NaN:NaN\", which is a quieter lie and was not in the original finding. React 19 unmounts the entire tree on an uncaught render throw, and reloading replays the same record from the log, so one poisoned durable event took the browser down permanently.\n\nTHE FIX, in two parts, and the second is the one that matters longer. isRenderableTimestamp gates the conversion: an unreadable time says so in the label and the tooltip, and no time element is emitted for a date that cannot supply a valid dateTime attribute. Separately a top-level ErrorBoundary contains any render failure — the next unpredicted throw now costs one subtree and a readable message instead of the session.\n\nONE DESIGN CHOICE TO PUSH BACK ON IF YOU DISAGREE. The boundary does not retry automatically. The projection is replayed from the log, so an automatic retry would loop on the same record forever; I gave the reader a button instead. The alternative is retrying once and then giving up, which I think is worse because it hides the determinism.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE, run not read. Removing the timestamp guard fails the out-of-range test; making the boundary pass its children through fails the containment test. Each fails only its own test, so the two guards are pinned separately.\n\nGates at this exact head: UI suite 81 of 81 with none skipped, npx tsc --noEmit clean, go vet, go build, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, pushed and matching, merges cleanly into main 50ebdead. The change is TypeScript only.\n\nConditions of bdb7d543, each met: safe fallback instead of a throw; a top-level error boundary; a UI test covering an out-of-range timestamp; the UI gate passing; a request branch and an exact head for review before any merge.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fadacd02c840b2c0efe76d77cc2ae68c070e4f89","conditions":"Report approved or changes-requested for exact head 2f028fbea208e661615b2028f2970bd0927e4309, naming artifact fadacd02 at ui, resting on your promise against THIS request; do not merge.","head":"2f028fbea208e661615b2028f2970bd0927e4309","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}